Scene background for the wild-battle screen — an open meadow combat arena in the same world as the hatch, register, and crew-showcase fields. Same painterly pixel-art rendering, warm palette, distant pine treeline, and soft rolling mountain silhouettes as hatch--day.png — not a flatter or more outlined sprite-sheet look. Match the hatch--day reference for golden-olive meadow tones, luminous sky gradients, and gentle dither shading on grass and trees.

Wide 16:9 horizontal landscape, camera zoomed in and angled slightly downward toward the ground; horizon around the vertical middle. This scene carries dense UI overlay (opponent HUD upper-left, player HUD mid-right, dialog bar lower-left, command menu lower-right) and two composited Vibemon sprites at runtime, so keep sky bands and the UI quadrants calm and low-contrast while the two battle rings read clearly.

Lighting: bright, warm golden midday — soft sunny daylight, gently saturated. A calm pale-blue and warm-cream daytime sky with a few soft clouds, kept especially soft and low-detail in the UPPER-LEFT quadrant for the opponent HUD plate. A thin low band of hazy distant pine treeline and soft rolling hills rests along the high horizon.

The grass field fills the lower two-thirds: lush golden-olive meadow with layered light and dark patches, individual blades catching warm sunny daylight, and a few tiny wildflowers scattered sparingly. Keep the broad center diagonal between the two rings open and uncluttered — this is the sightline projectiles travel across.

