- **Opponent ring (far, upper-right):** a smaller matching elliptical dirt patch in the upper-right midground — around 22–28% down from the top, inset from the right edge. Same trampled earth treatment but visibly smaller (roughly 6–7% of frame width) and slightly softer in contrast to sell distance. This is where the wild Vibemon stands, facing down-left toward the hero.
- The two rings sit on a diagonal axis (lower-left to upper-right), classic handheld battle staging. Grass grows up to the ring edges; do not merge the rings into one continuous dirt field. Keep both rings restrained — small battle pads, not large arenas.

Concentrate the busiest, highest-contrast grass tufts, wildflowers, and small rocks only along the extreme bottom foreground edge and in the far distance — not inside either ring or across the open center band. Keep the mid-right sky and lower-right grass soft for the player HUD and command menu overlays. No thick black or tobacco-brown outlines on grass, dirt, or trees; edges stay soft and atmospheric like the hatch reference.

